      "message": "fix(sim): sweep XY arcs on the true circle in the field engine and envelope scan\n\nThe field engine (field_cut::chords) and the generator-time envelope\nscan still drew G2/G3 in G17 as inscribed chords, a sagitta inside the\narc. That read false cuts at convex corners, and hid real cuts at\nconcave corners and on bull-nose helices, where a rim column the true\narc cuts 2.5 mm deep stood uncut on the field.\n\n- Field engine (new field_arc.rs): an upright mill tool's XY arc is\n  swept as Sweep::Arc pieces. The piece budget is unchanged, so the\n  windows and the cell ceiling are too. Level pieces are exact in\n  closed form (clamped bearing, the column's tie laws, closed-form\n  floor entry). Helical pieces use dexel_arc's sample + golden search,\n  with real evaluations only and the conservative hair.\n- Envelope scan (new scan_arc.rs): each arc piece keeps arc_chords'\n  chord for bins, boxes and rings. Every distance (rest, flank, hidden\n  rest, facet gouge) is read off the true arc, and walks and prunes\n  grow by the piece's bulge.\n- stock_bull_nose is back to 1e-5 engine parity on the helix arc.\n\nTilted poses, lathe tools and XZ/YZ arcs keep their chords.\n\nFixes #413\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
